---
import { siteConfig } from "../../../config";
import InformationLayout from "../../../layouts/InformationLayout.astro";
---

<InformationLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Drift handles Apple Music access, on-device data, website visits, and support communications."
  eyebrow="Drift for iOS"
  updated="Effective 1 August 2026"
  alternateHref="/zh-cn/drift/privacy/"
  alternateLabel="简体中文"
  canonicalPath="/drift/privacy/"
>
  <p class="lead">
    Drift ("the App") is a visual player for Apple Music developed by Oaky AI ("we", "us", or "our"). This Privacy Policy applies to the Drift iOS app and the related pages we operate. It explains what information is processed, why it is used, when it may be shared, your choices, and how to contact us.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can use Drift without creating an Oaky AI account. The current version does not maintain a developer-operated user account, analytics, or advertising system.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information we process</h2>

  <h3>1.1 Apple Music information</h3>
  <p>
    With your permission, Drift uses Apple's MusicKit framework to request information needed to provide its features. This may include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your Apple Music authorization status and subscription playback capabilities.</li>
    <li>Music library information such as playlists, albums, artists, songs, artwork, identifiers, and related metadata.</li>
    <li>Apple Music catalog recommendations, charts, new releases, artwork, availability, and playback resources.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Drift uses this information to generate visual music walls, display available selections, and play the music you choose. These requests are made through Apple's services. Oaky AI does not receive or store your Apple Music library on Oaky AI-operated servers.
  </p>

  <h3>1.2 Information stored locally</h3>
  <p>Drift stores limited information on your device to remember your choices and improve loading performance:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>App preferences, including playback order, title visibility, and wall speed.</li>
    <li>Cached music collection metadata, Apple Music item identifiers, and artwork.</li>
    <li>A temporary cached indication of Apple Music authorization and subscription playback availability.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Drift does not maintain its own listening-history or listening-statistics database. Apple may process playback activity as part of Apple Music under Apple's terms and privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h3>1.3 Support communications</h3>
  <p>
    If you contact us by email, we receive the email address you use and the information you choose to include, such as your device model, iOS version, app version, screenshots, and troubleshooting steps.
  </p>

  <h3>1.4 Website information</h3>
  <p>
    The Drift privacy and support pages are static. We do not place analytics, advertising, tracking scripts, account systems, or contact forms on these pages. Our hosting provider may process standard technical request information, such as an IP address, browser type, requested URL, and timestamp, as necessary to deliver and secure the website under its own terms and privacy practices.
  </p>

  <h3>1.5 Information we do not intentionally collect</h3>
  <p>The current version of Drift does not intentionally collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Contacts, precise location, photos, microphone content, or payment information.</li>
    <li>Apple Account passwords or other login credentials.</li>
    <li>Advertising identifiers or data for cross-app tracking.</li>
    <li>Data for third-party analytics, advertising, or profiling.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
  <p>Information is processed only as needed to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Authorize Apple Music access and determine whether playback is available.</li>
    <li>Load your music library and Apple Music discovery content.</li>
    <li>Display artwork and metadata and play music you select.</li>
    <li>Remember app preferences and improve repeat loading through local caching.</li>
    <li>Diagnose problems, reply to support messages, and maintain Drift.</li>
    <li>Protect the App and website and comply with applicable law.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Information sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell or rent personal information. We do not use Drift's local data for advertising or ad profiling. Information may be processed or disclosed only in the following circumstances.
  </p>

  <h3>3.1 At your direction</h3>
  <p>
    Information is used or disclosed when you initiate an action, such as authorizing Apple Music, choosing a song to play, opening an external link, or sending a support email.
  </p>

  <h3>3.2 Apple services</h3>
  <p>
    Drift relies on MusicKit and Apple Music for authorization, subscription status, library and catalog requests, artwork, and playback. Apple processes information required to provide these services under Apple's terms and privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h3>3.3 Necessary infrastructure providers</h3>
  <p>
    Website hosting and email providers process the limited information needed to deliver the public website and support email. Their processing is governed by their respective terms and privacy practices.
  </p>

  <h3>3.4 Legal and safety reasons</h3>
  <p>
    We may preserve or disclose information when reasonably necessary to comply with applicable law, regulation, court order, or lawful government request, or to protect the rights, safety, and property of users, the public, Oaky AI, or others.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Data storage, retention, and security</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>App preferences, cached metadata, and artwork are stored on your device.</li>
    <li>You can clear cached content from Drift's Storage settings.</li>
    <li>Depending on your device and backup settings, some local app data may be included in Apple-managed backups.</li>
    <li>Removing Drift removes its locally stored app data, subject to normal iOS and backup behavior.</li>
    <li>Support correspondence is retained only as reasonably necessary to respond, maintain support records, prevent abuse, resolve disputes, or comply with legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use reasonable measures appropriate to the limited information we handle. However, no method of storage or electronic transmission is completely secure, and email should not be used to send passwords, payment information, or other unnecessary sensitive information.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your choices and rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Apple Music access:</strong> You can grant or revoke Drift's permission in iOS Settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Local preferences:</strong> You can change available playback and visual settings inside Drift.</li>
    <li><strong>Cache:</strong> You can clear cached metadata and artwork from Drift's Storage settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> You can remove locally stored app data by deleting Drift, subject to normal iOS backup behavior.</li>
    <li><strong>Support information:</strong> You may contact us to request access to, correction of, or deletion of information you previously sent to us, subject to applicable law and legitimate retention needs.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, applicable law may provide additional privacy rights. Contact us to make a request or raise a complaint. We may need enough information to verify and respond to the request.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Drift is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. Apple Music eligibility, family settings, and content restrictions are managed through the user's Apple services and device settings.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect product changes, legal requirements, or regulatory guidance. The updated version will be published on this page with a revised effective date. We will provide additional notice when appropriate for a material change.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact us</h2>
  <p>For privacy questions, comments, complaints, or requests, contact Oaky AI at:</p>
  <a class="contact-link" href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a>
</InformationLayout>
